  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Imperfect gerundio",
   "texto": [
    "The imperfect gerunde expresses a simultaneous action with that of the main verb. It is formed from the present theme with **-а/-я**; the 3rd plural person helps to recognize the base: **читают → чита- → читая**, **слушают → слуша- → слушая**, **работают → работа- → работая**. There are exceptions and root changes.",
    "In the usual construction, the gerundio is the same subject that performs the main verb: **Читая книгу, я пью чай** (I read and I drink tea).",
    "Posture forms such as **сидя** («sitting down») and **стоя** («standing») can also work as adverbs; here they express a simultaneous action of the same subject."
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Perfect gerundio",
   "texto": [
    "The perfect gerunde expresses an action prior to the main. **-в** and **-вши** are common: **написать → написав**, **вернуться → вернувшись**; some roots have special forms, such as **прийти → придя**.",
    "Here too the subject must match: **Придя домой, я обедаю** (I arrive and I have lunch). It avoids phrases where it seems that the gerunde is another person."
   ]
  },
